.TH FSLEDGERD 8 "2026-10-02" "fsledger" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fsledgerd \- foreground filesystem history daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fsledgerd
.RB [ \-c " configuration" ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.br
.B fsledgerd \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
fsledgerd runs the same pipeline as
.BR "fsledger run" .
It remains in the foreground; the service manager provides supervision.
Multiple repositories may run concurrently, but mirror and Git operations are
serialized within each repository. Unknown actors never block a commit.
Both Git and DB repositories maintain an integrity catalog. Only Git
repositories
copy file contents and create commits. Report preparation and notification
delivery
run independently of the repository's copy and commit worker.
Configured sources that do not exist are skipped and adopted when they appear;
see paths in
.BR fsledger.yaml (5).
.PP
Files changing during observation are retried up to three times. Persistently
unstable paths retain their previous valid copies while other changes can be
committed. Pending paths appear in the status field unstable_paths and are
retried
by a reconciliation scheduled after one minute, even if periodic reconciliation
is disabled. Polling with a scan cron waits for its next configured scan slot
instead. An incomplete inventory cannot initialize an integrity baseline.
.PP
Explicit polling reuses the full repository scanner and inventory, without
fanotify/inotify marks or passive Audit attribution. Interval or cron schedules
can control ordinary traversal and full hashing independently. For polling,
watch.reconcile.on_start=false defers initial observation and on_stop=false
omits shutdown traversal. Both options default to true. Changes reverted between
scans may be missed, and periodic observations do not identify their writer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " configuration"
YAML configuration path; default /etc/fsledger/fsledger.yaml.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Override the YAML log level with debug, retaining its destination.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Display option help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version, Git commit and Go toolchain, then exit without reading
the configuration.
.SH OPENRC
Install with make install-openrc, review the YAML, then enable and start:
.nf
rc-update add fsledger default
rc-service fsledger start
rc-service fsledger checkconfig
rc-service fsledger status
rc-service fsledger stop
.fi
.PP
/etc/conf.d/fsledger selects the configuration with fsledger_config.
The service uses supervise-daemon, waits for local mounts and orders after
available network mounts. It validates the configuration before starting;
absent sources are skipped. It allows
300 seconds after SIGTERM before sending SIGKILL; the daemon uses a 270-second
grace from SIGTERM, including the operation already running. Blocked filesystem
I/O may exceed that deadline.
When SIGTERM interrupts a reconciliation, the final reconciliation is skipped
because the next startup reconciliation resumes the work. Adjust the init
script for filesystems that can block longer. Use logging.file for persistent
daemon logs.
.SH SYSTEMD
Install with make install-systemd, review the YAML, then run:
.nf
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl enable --now fsledger
journalctl -u fsledger -f
.fi
.PP
The unit permits the default state, runtime and /var/log/fsledger log
directory.
Custom writable locations require corresponding unit overrides. It allows 300
seconds for shutdown. Sources are read-only under ProtectSystem=strict; optional
bidirectional Git requires explicit ReadWritePaths for authorized sources.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGINT and SIGTERM trigger orderly shutdown, including pending Git work.
SIGHUP logs an info notice only; restart to reload YAML or reopen a rotated
log.
.SH SECURITY
The default service runs as root to observe privileged source paths and use
fanotify. Sources never receive Git metadata. Mirrors and logs should be
private.
Audit is passive: fsledgerd never installs rules, enables Audit, or takes the
controller role from auditd. Administrator rules must cover the desired
sources.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on clean shutdown, help or version; 1 on configuration, startup or runtime
error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fsledger (1),
.BR fsledger.yaml (5),
.BR openrc-run (8),
.BR supervise-daemon (8)
